  "review_notes": [
    "מֵעֵבֶר לְ is taken as a single fused unit under rule 30's compound-preposition clause; the competing reading splits the לְ off as the preposition governing *the Jordan* and marks it unrepresented, but *beyond* carries every morpheme's sense, so nothing is left over.",
    "The he of יַהְצָה is fused with the name rather than marked unrepresented, since the ASV's *Jahzah* spells it out."
